WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.001 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
Thank you for having me.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We are so happy
to have you here.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:06.006
I have -- I think a lot of
people have really enjoyed

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.608
watching this new wave of people
come into Congress.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.476 line:92%
Of course, you're one of them.

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.611 size:81% position:41%
And one of the things
I particularly enjoyed

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:15.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
watching you do is
ask people questions

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.116 size:88% position:44% line:92%
on Congressional panels.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:18.551
Now, this is not something
you had experience with.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:21.821
You famously did not have
any experience in politics

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
before this job.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.090
Why do you think it is that you
are good at it

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.794
and do you think anything you
did that was outside of politics

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
has been helpful?

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:30.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think
one thing is that --

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:33.900
I was reflecting because --
I was just reflecting today

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
because exactly a year ago,
I was working in a restaurant.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:38.805 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was bartending.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:43.476
And I think that that proximity,
just being a real working person

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:47.180
in the halls of Congress
is actually such a jarring

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.450 size:88% position:44%
difference from who has
historically been there,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:54.654
that it really allows you to cut
through the BS super quickly

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:58.958
and -- especially with someone
who had to, you know, close up

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:03.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
a restaurant at night and have
to kick everyone out, like,

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're really good at just
saying, "Hey. Enough."

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.370 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It strikes me --
you know, oftentimes

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're given five minutes
to ask questions

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're given someone who,
obviously, if given time,

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:18.945 line:92%
you'd want to ask a lot more of.

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
It strikes me
some of you go in with a plan.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
You strike me
as one of those people.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is true of
a lot of other Democrats

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:26.986
as well as many Republicans,
come in with no plan at all.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:29.589
When you're sitting there,
are you often taken aback by

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
how bad they are
at asking questions?

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:31.691 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:37.330
-Well, sometimes, especially
with my Republican colleagues,

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.898 line:92%
they say things and I'm like,

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:42.402
"What does that have to do with
what we're talking about?"

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:44.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's this one member
who famously,

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:48.408
every single Financial Services
Committee hearing,

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.176 line:92%
he says, "I ask everyone this --

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:53.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
are you a capitalist
or a socialist?"

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.481 line:92%
And the person's in charge of

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
national flood
insurance program.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:57.984 size:78% position:39% line:92%
They're like, "What?"

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:58.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:02.522
-And the best thing, too, is
this -- you know, last week,

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:07.193
he actually said, "Are you
a capitalist or a socialist?

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:07.694 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yes or no?"

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:10.797
And the woman said, "Yes or no?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.165 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And he says, "Yeah."

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.600 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And she goes, "Yes."

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.635 line:92%
And it was the whole panel --

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:19.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he made everyone go down
and everyone said,

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.773 size:88% position:44% line:92%
yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:21.307 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:24.944
And then I said, "Hey, it's
great. We have a mixed economy.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:25.545 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's possible."

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.981 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah, you don't know
which one they are.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which one they were
saying yes to.

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:32.685
One obsession, or I should say,
a group of people

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
that seem to have an obsession
with you

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.389 line:92%
is our friends over at Fox News.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-They talk about you a lot.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:41.594
Are you surprised with the speed
at which they seem to have

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:45.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
shifted all their attention
and programming to you?

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.266 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I mean, it's weird.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.934 line:92%
Like, why are so many grown men

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:51.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
just obsessed with
this 29-year-old?

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's great.
I love the --

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:58.011 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:58.845 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I mean...

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:01.281 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-On second thought.

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, but I think
it's really funny,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the conspiracy theories
are great.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:09.055
-Yeah, well today, Mike Huckabee
said that there are --

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:12.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
he did that great thing that
people on Fox News do

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:12.592 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
which he said,

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:15.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Some people are saying
she's a Manchurian candidate.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:15.662 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know."

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:18.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which is a super classy thing
to do.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:22.635
If you don't know, Mike Huckabee
is a famous bass player.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:23.203 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you -- Just since
I have you here,

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:27.040 line:92%
are you a Manchurian candidate?

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:27.473 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm not.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.576
-That's exactly what a
Manchurian candidate would say.

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:31.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:31.844 line:92%
-That's exactly. Caught you.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:36.082
-Not a Manchurian candidate,
but I do have amazing staff,

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
and in no part
thanks to the fact

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:40.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we pay a living wage
in our office.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.323 size:78% position:39%
We don't pay any less
than $52,000 a year.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:46.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which means --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:50.897
-Which means so far two of my
staffers have been able to quit

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:54.434
their second jobs in restaurants
and be fully present at work.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:57.737
And so, you know, I hope
it's a lesson to our folks

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.239 line:92%
on the other side of the aisle

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
that if you pay your staff,
then --

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:03.610 size:75% position:38%
-You'll be prepared.
-You'll be prepared.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:08.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
You won't be saying yes or no,
capitalism or socialism.

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:09.282 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:10.683 line:92%
-One thing I'm curious about,

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
because obviously
a lot of people,

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:14.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
your colleagues
across the aisle,

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
they also consume
a lot of Fox News.

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:18.891
Do they then get, you know,
bad information about you?

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:21.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
And how has your interaction
with them been so far?

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:22.262 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:26.899
Well, it is funny because one of
the side effects of kind of

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:33.640
this Fox News lunacy is that
other actual members of Congress

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
believe it
and see it uncritically.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:40.179
And so I was on the floor once,
and this guy came up to me

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:40.713 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and he was like,

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:43.816
"Is it true that you got
$10 million from Netflix?"

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:46.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "No."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:50.556
It was, like, in the well. Like,
we're voting on gun reform.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:54.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like,
"What else do you not know?"

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.528 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:56.596 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is concerning.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:05:00.733 size:88% position:44%
-He said, "Did you make
$10 million or no money,

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:04.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
yes or no?
-Yes. Exactly.

